# Example only. Do not copy this file. start.ps1 makes the real one on the first run:
#     %USERPROFILE%\.kaggle-coder\.env      (outside the game folder, never uploaded to GitHub)
# Never put a real key or token in this example file: it goes to GitHub.
# Your Kaggle API token is separate. It goes in %USERPROFILE%\.kaggle\access_token (setup.cmd does this).

# Your helper key. Made for you on the first run (32 or more letters and numbers). Nothing to do.
# CODER_API_KEY=made-for-you-by-start.ps1

# OPTIONAL permanent address. Leave these out and the free temporary address is used.
# fixed-address.cmd fills them in for you (steps: fixed-address\README.md).
# FIXED_HOST=kaggle.gamelab.link
# CF_ACCOUNT_ID=your-cloudflare-account-id
# CF_KV_NAMESPACE_ID=your-kv-namespace-id
# CF_KV_TOKEN=a-token-that-can-only-edit-that-one-store

# OPTIONAL timers (defaults shown; leave them out unless you want to change them).
# IDLE_MINUTES=10        turn the AI off after this many minutes without a question (5 to 60)
# BLOCK_MINUTES=ask      ask at each start "how long will you code?" (30, 45 or 60). Or set 0 (never ask,
#                        just use the idle rule) or a number to always use that coding block.
#                        During a block the AI stays up through quiet pauses. After it, IDLE_MINUTES applies again.
